dns.c: include <resolv.h> for getrrsetbyname / struct rrsetinfo.

OpenSSH's dns.c assumes that when HAVE_GETRRSETBYNAME is defined the
function and its rrsetinfo type are visible via <netdb.h>, which is
true on OpenBSD/NetBSD but not on Linux/glibc nor on substrate.
Substrate's libresolv exports them through <resolv.h>; include that
explicitly so HAVE_GETRRSETBYNAME=yes is enough to skip the
openbsd-compat fallback.

--- a/dns.c
+++ b/dns.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <sys/socket.h>
 #include <netdb.h>
+#include <resolv.h>
 #include <stdarg.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <string.h>
